From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150: add the 2.9568 GHz prime CPU OPP

The SM8150-AB variant used on the OnePlus 7T advertises one more prime
core level in its hardware frequency LUT than the table in sm8150.dtsi
describes.  qcom-cpufreq-hw does not add operating points, it only
adjusts the voltage of an existing one, so the extra level is dropped:

  cpu cpu7: Voltage update failed freq=2956800
  cpu cpu7: failed to update OPP for freq=2956800

and the prime core stays at 2.8416 GHz.  Add the missing operating point;
the voltage is still programmed from the hardware LUT at runtime, so the
entry only needs the frequency and the interconnect bandwidth.

Signed-off-by: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
@@ -606,6 +606,11 @@
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <2841600000>;
 			opp-peak-kBps = <8368000 51609600>;
 		};
+
+		cpu7_opp21: opp-2956800000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <2956800000>;
+			opp-peak-kBps = <8368000 51609600>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	firmware {
